N2  - The proceedings contain 96 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Neuroscience. The topics include: Exploring the effect of melatonin on peripheral neuropathy in experimental diabetic rats by electrodermal activity; investigation the effects of memantine and melatonin treatment after traumatic brain injury in rats; effect of melatonin administration on pain threshold in hypertonic saline-induced myalgia model of exercise trained rats; anterior insular self-regulation in obsessive compulsive disorder using real-time functional magnetic resonance imaging; default mode network connectivity persistence during a motor paradigm; epileptic seizures-induced structural changes in rat spine tissues; hippocampal place cell activity is correlated with the future position of freely moving rats; epigenetic evaluation of the effects of alcohol on the fetal brain development; insight into hippocampus development during the first two postnatal months in control and fetal alcohol rats; gene expression changes in aging zebrafish (danio rerio) brains across lifespan; effects of resveratrol and resveratrol delivered in liposome on penicilin-induced brain epileptic activity in male rats; oxygen-glucose-deprivation-related neurodegeneration in acute brain slices and pharmacological applications; volumetric changes in magnetic resonance imaging in patients with major depressive disorder; serum anti-neuronal antibodies in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis; N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor NR1-NR2 subunit expression in hyperplastic thymus of an autoimmune encephalitis patient; ion channel and synapse antibodies for differential diagnosis of chronic neurodegenerative and psychiatric disorders; the relationship between oxidative stress and Bcl-2 in hippocampus of middle-aged rats; the relationship between oxidative stres and Sirt2 in serebral cortex of middle-aged; the effects of ingested sulfite on hippocampal oxidant/antioxidant capacities and activities of phospholipase A2 enzymes; increased risk of cardiovaskuler risk factors in psychiatric disorders; effect of cycloastragenol against amyloid beta toxicity; effects of maternally exposed food colourings on neurobehaviour in offspring; possible contribution of sulfite molecule on homocysteine toxicity in neuroblastoma cell line; antidepressant effects of infralimbic cortex ROCK inhibition in rats; spinal schwannoma case with atipic syptoms; chronic escitalopram treatment prevents long-term neuroplasticity impairment that develops in REM deprivation; subcellular translocation of Elk-1 protein upon hypoxia; effect of Pea3 transcription factor on differentiation of motor neurons; effects of antidepressants on contractile responses in rat aorta; effect of CDP-choline on disruption of prepulse inhibition (PPI) which is one of the biological markers of schizophrenia; the effect of mesenchymal stem cell transplantation in neuropathic mice; neural differentiation on bioactive peptide nanofiber scaffolds; feeding behavior might affect circadian rhythms with phase shift in gerbils; a bioloid robot implementation of computational basal ganglia circuit; the evaluation of pain threshold and behaviour in visceral pain model on rats; the effect of alcohol on MeCP2 protein during cerebral cortex development; the evaluation of pain threshold and behaviour in neuropathic pain model on rats; dose dependent effect of lidocaine on the nerve conduction rate of rat sciatic nerve; the efficiency of melatonin against peripheral neuropathy in streptozotocin induced diabetic rats; large-scale automated analysis of neuronal calcium transients; the mediation of central histaminergic receptors in arachidonic acid induced cardiovascular effects; effect of valproic acid on motor function in 6-hydroxydopamine treated parkinsonian rats; the relationship between cerebral lateralization and cardiac autonomic activity; application of new generation sequencing method for SCN1A screening; effects of mental stress on the control mechanisms of cutaneous blood flow; the effects of chronic escitalopram treatment on memory and mood changes in REM sleep deprivation; gender dependency of spatial memory in experimental hyperthyroidism model; effects of alpha-lipoic acid and N-acetylcysteine on acrylamide-induced toxicity; gender dimorphism induced by cold environment in hippocampal functions; the effects of neural circuits and biochemicals on human reasoning and decision making process; effects of different doses of carnosine on the sympathetic skin response and anxiety; impairment of hippocampal long-term potentiation by aluminum exposure in adult rats; kernel-based approaches for accurate spike sorting; interhemispheric transfer time in developmental dyslexia; effects of simvastatin on experimental neuropathic pain model and the role of nitric oxide; the investigation of the antinociceptive effect and mechanisms of action of acute curcumin application in mice; effects of kisspeptin infusion and aromatase inhibition on cognitive functions and behavior in female rats; effect of medication on auditory processing disorder and attention deficit disorder; the effect of magnetic field to VEGF and HIF-1 expression in hippocampus in febrile convulsive rats; effect of melatonin on substantia nigra cyclooxygenase, caspase-3, nuclear factor kappa-B in experimental Parkinson and the investigation of predisposition to psychosis in rat model of sepsis.
