N2  - We report a 46-year-old male infected with Coxiella burnetii, complaining of slight fever, general fatigue, and trouble sleeping. Minocycline therapy for 3 months relieved his symptoms, including a depressive state, resulting in thoughts of death. This case is the first report on post-Q fever fatigue syndrome associated with depression. © 2012 Japan International Cultural Exchange Foundation & Japan Health Sciences University.
