N2  - The proceedings contain 83 papers. The topics discussed include: effect of human equilibrative nucleoside transporter 1 (hENT1) expression on adenosine production from neurons; validation of the novel in vitro platelet toxicity assay (iPTA) for the diagnosis of drug hypersensitivity reactions; role of efflux transporter P-glycoprotein (MDR1) in rivaroxaban drug disposition; limited placental transfer of 6-mercaptopurine is mediated by tissue binding and not active transport; ncidence of central nervous system (CNS) depression of neonates breastfed by mothers receiving oxycodone for postpartum analgesia; effects of chronic renal failure on brain drug transporters in rats; repeated ethanol exposure of fetal sheep in late gestation and fatty acid ethyl esters in meconium; and thiopurine methyltransferase and inosine triphosphate pyrophosphohydrolase genotypes among patients with inflammatory bowel disease treated with azathioprine.
