N2  - Mental disorders such as depression or schizophrenia are abundant in the western world. Therefore a simple and reliable LC-MS/MS method for therapeutic drug monitoring was developed and validated. To 200 μ l of serum, 20 μ l of a 25 % vitamin C solution as well as 30 μ l of an internal standard solution were added. After centrifugation, the supernatant was transferred into an autosampler vial. Extraction was performed online using a Cyclone turbulent flow column (Thermo Fisher Scientific, Switzerland) and an Interchim C18 column (Interchim, France) for the analytical separation. The mobile phases consisted of ammonium acetate, acetonitrile, methanol and formic acid. The analytes were separated into 4 different runs according to their chemical properties. For runs 1, 2 and 3, APCI was used for the ionization, whereas in run 4, HESI was used. All analytes were detected in positive mode on a triple stage quadrupole MS (TSQ Quantum Access Max, Thermo Fisher Scientific, Switzerland) in the SRM mode. The method was linear in the range of 1-50 μ g/l (flupenthixol, fluphenazine), 5-250 μ g/l (duloxetine, norsertraline, reboxetine, sertindole, sertraline, zuclopenthixol), 10-500 μ g/l (amisulpride, clomipramine, chlorpromazine, chlorprothixene, clotiapine, desipramine, desmethyltrimipramine, dibenzepin, doxepin, imipramine, levomepromazine, mCPP, maprotiline, mianserine, nordoxepin, nortriptyline, opipramol, pipamperon, promazine, trimipramine) and 50-2500 μ g/l (amitriptyline, desmethylclomipramine, moclobemide, trazodone), according to their therapeutic range. Within-day and between-day precision was < 9.47 % for all analytes and the respective accuracy was in the range of 90.5-109 % . No matrix effects could be detected and the variation of the recovery was < 15 % between the 3 tested concentrations. A simple and accurate LC-MS/MS method was developed and validated for the quantification of 32 antidepressant and antipsychotic drugs.
