N2  - Objectives: To estimate the influence of viscosupplementation with hyaluronic acid (HA) on the quality of life (QoL) next 6 month in patients with knee osteoarthritis (OA). Materials/Methods: 75 eligible patients with verified diagnosis of knee osteoarthritis (Kellgren Lawrence grade from I to IV). Depending on the stage two groups were formed: 1-with I-II OA grade (n=37), 2-with III and IV grade (n=38). In line with the manufacturer's recommendations all subjects received a course of 5 weekly intraarticular injection of FERMATHRON (1,100-1,400 kDa HA, 20 mg/2.0 ml). Quality of life was assessed with a SF-36 Score at preinjection, at 3 and 6 month after treatment. Results: As expected, the baseline mean values of SF-36 proved to beworse in 2 group's patients. Analysis demonstrated significant differences of primary physical functioning (mean±sd, 56.4±26.1 in 1 group, 25.9±20.6 in 2 group, p<0.001) and mental health (62.1±17.4 vs. 49.9±18.6, p<0.02). In both groups mean bodily pain were significantly reduced 3 and 6 months after the last injection. Thus, in group 1 pain level was 25.5±21.9 at 3 months and 23.9±18.5 at 6 months starting at 44.1±14.8, p<0.005 compared to 42.2± 15 and 47.9±14.2 vs. 60±17.3, p<0.02 in 2 group respectively. There was significant impairment of social functioning in patients of 1 group at 6 month (46.2±10.7 vs. 58.2±15.4, p<0.01) and not significant depression of rolephysical functioning in 2 group at the same time (16±5.4 vs. 18.5±12.9). The data obtained from every participant have shown not significant progress of all estimated parameters over the observation. Overall physical health and mental health at baseline and during all monitoring had no significant differences both between groups and within groups. Conclusions: The viscosupplementation with HA in Russians patients with knee OA led to a significant pain reduction and a slight improvement of their life's quality. However, significant effect on the overall physical health and mental health not found yet. To improve general QoL should be employ a comprehensive therapy, including social rehabilitation and patients' adaptation.
