N2  - Cytokines have been related to depression by numerous studies. These have in general shown that cytokine function is impaired in the presence of depression. For example we have shown that hostility and severity of depressive symptoms, separately and jointly. Impair the capacity of blood monocytes to secrete an array of cytokines when stimulated by bacterial lipopolysaccharide (LPS). Higher Beck Depression Inventory scores were associated with greater expression of TNF-alpha (beta=0.042, p=0.02) and IL-8 (beta=0.045, p=0.04). This led us to study if Etanercept a TNF antagonist will improve depression. 618 patients with moderate to severe psoriasis received double-blind treatment with placebo or 50 mg twice-weekly Etanercept. The Hamilton rating scale for depression (Ham-D), the Beck depression inventory (BDI), were used to assess depression. Greater proportions of patients receiving etanercept had at least a 50% improvement in Ham-D or BDI at week 12 compared with the placebo group. Improvements in symptoms of depression were less correlated with objective measures of skin clearance or joint pain. Etanercept treatment might relieve symptoms of depression associated with chronic inflammatory disease. These studies suggest that further evaluation of cytokine based treatments is worthwhile.
