N2  - The proceedings contain 179 papers. The topics discussed include: analysis of secular trends and impact of clostridium difficile in hospitalized children with inflammatory bowel disease; need for rescue therapy in IBD patients on infliximab maintenance therapy after discontinuation of immunomodulator; is isotretinoin exposure associated with inflammatory bowel disease? a case control study; relationship between depressive severity and demographics in youth with inflammatory bowel disease; the association between IBD and venous thromboembolic events in Danish children and adults: a population-based case-control study; characterizing depression in children with inflammatory bowel disease; improved outcomes in a quality improvement collaborative for pediatric Crohn disease; immunogenicity of influenza vaccination in children with inflammatory bowel disease; and refractory clostridium difficile infection masking undiagnosed ulcerative colitis.
