N2  - Somatopsychic disorders at first anxiety and depression are very frequent in chronically and incurable ill patients. Several factors (genetic vulnerability, history of advanced psychiatric diseases, personality, several forms of somatic treatment) are involved in the etiology. The possibility of adverse events of prescribed medications like chemotherapeutics, antibiotics and steroids must be considered. Psychopharmacological, psychotherapeutic and social treatment methods are possible interventions. Regarding pharmacotherapy, antidepressants with co-analgetic potency (i.e. SSNRI) are prefered, side effects and possible interactions with other drugs must be observed, however. Psychotherapeutic interventions include cognitive-behavioral techniques as well as coping strategies. Close contact to the next relatives is essential, professional help should be offered possibly. Controlled studies are missing in this field so far and are needed urgently.
