N2  - Research on the pathophysiology of NCCP has revealed that acid is not the only cause of pain in this population. Studies of motility disorders, the composition of the refluxate, central mechanisms involved in esophageal hypersensitivity, and the role of psychosocial comorbidity have enhanced our understanding of the origin of chest pain of esophageal origin. However, further research is required, especially to elucidate the nociceptive neural pathways involved in esophageal hypersensitivity, and to clarify the role of psychological factors like anxiety and depression on the esophageal perception. No doubt this will eventually provide new opportunities in the treatment of this challenging disorder. © 2008 Mosby, Inc. All rights reserved.
