N2  - Psoriasis is a chronic inflammatory skin disease which often requires lifelong treatment. Many patients suffering from psoriasis report dissatisfaction from traditional antipsoriatic therapies, because they are often not enough effective, they provide only temporal improvement and may be responsible for considerable side-effects, especially at long-term usage. The vast majority of psoriatic subjects demonstrate significantly diminished health-related quality of life (HRQoL). Introduction of biologic agents begun a new era of immunopathogenic targeted therapies for psoriasis. These drugs seem to be of special usefulness for patient who did not respond or have contraindication to other systemic therapies. Because of high efficacy and favorable safety profile, they may be used for a very long period of time without significant risk of side effects. Etanercept is a soluble tumor necrosis factor α receptor approved for the treatment of plaque psoriasis and psoriatic arthritis. Etanercept has been proven to be highly effective in the treatment of psoriasis. Several reports also documented, that the therapy with etanercept significantly improves patients' quality of life (QoL). Recent meta-analysis on the effect of biologicals on QoL in psoriatics revealed, that among all approved biologic agents for the treatment of psoriasis the greatest improvement of HRQoL was noted in etanercept and infliximab group. Over 60% improvement of Dermatology Life Quality Index was noted at week 12 compared to baseline in patients receiving 50 mg of etanercept per week. Moreover, etanercept treatment also reduced fatigue and symptoms of depression associated with psoriasis. Copyright © 2007 Cornetis.
