N2  - A five-month-old boy was submitted with fever and developed signs of meningitis. Spinal fluid analysis showed signs of bacterial meningitis. The patient was treated with ampicillin/ ceftriaxone i.v. Seven to eight hours after the termination of antibiotic therapy, the meningitis recurred. A haemangioma with a central depression was noted in the midline lumbosacral region. MRI showed a dorsal dermal sinus and intraspinal lipoma in the lumbar region. The patient underwent surgery and was subsequently treated with antibiotics for three weeks. Cutaneous signs of dorsal dermal sinus should cause early referral to MRI.
