N2  - General pharmacological properties of osutidine* ((±)-N-[(E)- [(p, β- dihydroxyphenethyl)amino][[2-[[5- [(methylamino)methyl]furfuryl]thio]ethyl]amino]methylene]methanesulfonamide, T-593), a novel antiulcer agent, were investigated using several animal species. T-593, at 1,000 mg/kg p.o., prolonged the pentobarbital-induced sleeping time in mice. It had no effects on general behavior, spontaneous motor activity, muscle tone, motor coordination, convulsions and acetic acid- induced writhing in mice, body temperature and spinal reflex in rats, and electroencephalogram in rabbits. T-593, at more than 10 mg/kg i.v., produced a transient decrease in blood pressure, increased the heart rate and respiratory rate in anesthetized dogs or rabbits. The depression of ST, reduced amplitude of QRS and extrasystole in ECG were also observed at 10 mg/kg or more. T-593, at 30 mg/kg i.v., inhibited the contraction of nictitating membrane induced by pre-ganglionic stimulation in cats, and at 10-4 g/ml, showed a slight inhibition of acetylcholine-induced contraction of isolated ileum and an enhancement of epinephrine-induced contraction of isolated vas deferens from guinea pigs. T-593, at more than 10 mg/kg i.v., inhibited a spontaneous motility of rabbit ileum in situ, and at 10-4 g/ml slightly inhibited the motility of isolated ileum from rabbits. It had no effects on intestinal propulsive motility in mice, and gastric output and bile secretion in rats. T-593, at 1,000 mg/kg p.o., decreased the urinary volume and electrolytes excretion (K+, Cl-), increased the PSP excretion in rats, and inhibited the collagen-induced platelet aggregation by 8% in rats. T-593, at 1,000 mg/kg p.o., showed a weak anti-inflammatory activity in rats. It had no effects on neuromuscular junction in rats, corneal reflex in rabbits and hepatic drug-metabolizing enzyme activity in mice. These results demonstrate that T-593 exerts general pharmacological effects only at high doses or high concentrations under the experimental conditions reported.
