N2  - Conditioned mediums prepared from explants of the fibrous membrane in aseptically loosened cemented total joint arthroplasties were added to cultures of an osteoblast-like cell line (UMR 106). Cellular activities were assessed after ten hours of incubation by means of protein production, alkaline phosphatase, acid phosphatase and tritiated thymidine uptake. A depression effect on the cells was observed. This phenomenon was partially reversed by indomethacin, thus implying the role of prostaglandins, although other factors could also be involved.
