N2  - Clinical and canine studies of the cardiovascular response to severe bacterial infection have shown reversible myocardial depression (decreased left ventricular ejection fraction) and left ventricular dilation producing a high or normal cardiac output. Conventional treatment includes antibiotics and cardiovascular support. Therapies aimed at neutralizing septic shock toxins are currently being evaluated.
