N2  - Sepsis causes significant morbidity in trauma patients and is the premiere cause of death in the period following initial injury. A multifactorial depression of humoral and cell-mediated immunity occurs soon after trauma. Loss of skin integrity, surgical procedures, invasive prosthetic devices, medications and colonization with virulent organisms further predispose these patients to infection. The liberal use of antibiotics should be discouraged in trauma patients to minimize superinfection with resistant organisms.
