N2  - The myocardial depressant action of aminoglycosides has been known for years but data on newer derivatives are currently not available. We have studied the contractile responses of isolated guinea-pig left atria to increasing concentrations of gentamicin, sissomicin, netilmicin, ribomycin and spectinomycin (0.02, 0.04, 0.08, 0.13, 0.17 and 0.22 mM). Our results are in keeping with those of previous investigators demonstrating that newer aminoglycosides do exert a similar depressant action. Netilmicin was more depressant than gentamicin and sissomicin, then ribomycin at similar concentrations while spectinomycin did not exert any effect at all. However this myocardial depression is obtained using concentrations far exceeding those reached in clinical practice. The status of netilmicin is somewhat less favourable.
