N2  - Start with paracetamol, acetylsalicylic acid, or phenazone (antipyrine) 0.5-1 g 3-4 times daily. When the pain is more intense, combine paracetamol or acetylsalicylic acid 1 g with codeine 30-60 g 4 times daily, paracetamol or acetylsalicylic acid 1 g with pentazocine 25-50 mg 4-6 times daily, or phenazone (antipyrine) 1 g with dextropropoxyphene napsylate 100 mg or dextropropoxyphene chloride 70 mg 3 times daily. Add to these, especially for insomnia, night pain, or low pain tolerance, amitriptyline or trimipramine 25-100 mg and possible levomepromazine 5-25 mg in the evening. Anxiety and depression should be treated with a tricyclic antidepressant with a dimethylamino group 25-100 mg in the evening, or fluphenazine, haloperidol, flupenthixol 0.5-1 mg twice daily or chlorprothixene 5-15 mg 3 times daily. These patients must avoid daily use of benzodiazepines, barbiturates and alcohol.
