N2  - Start with paracetamol, acetysalicylic acid, or phenazone (antipyrine) 1 g 3-4 times daily. When necessary, add codeine 30-100 mg, pentazocine 25-100 mg, or dextropropoxyphene napsylate 100-200 mg (or dextropropoxyphene chloride 70-140 mg) 4 times daily. For anxiety, depression, insomnia or night pain add amitriptyline or trimipramine 25-50 mg and levomepromazine 5-25 mg in the evening. For severe anxiety or panic reaction, give diazepam 5-15 mg intravenously or orally 3-4 times daily. Severe cancer pain unrelieved by other means: Pain cocktail with methadone 5, 10, 20 and up to 40 mg added to 20 ml of paracetamol solution given orally 4-6 times daily for 2-4 days, thereafter 3-4 times daily. Methadone may be replaced with morphine in doses from 10 to 90 mg in 20 ml solution, but a morphine pain cocktail must be given regularly every 4 hours. When oral medication is impossible, 50-75% of the methadone dose or 25% of the morphine dose should be given intramuscularly. Give prednisone 5-10 mg 3 times daily or naproxene 250 mg twice daily for painful bone metastases. Give haloperidol, fluphenazine, or flupenthixol 0.5-1 mg 2-3 times daily for hallucinations. Give prochlorperazine 5-10 mg 4 times daily or levomepromazine 10-25 mg in the evening for nausea. When the patient is suffering from severe depression or apathy, try cocaine chloride 10 mg orally 3 times daily.
