N2  - Treatment of radiation affections of the urinary tract presents considerable difficulties due to profound destructive-degenerative changes in their wall and depression of repair processes in tissues. The authors report on the successful treatment of 158 patients with various radiation affections of the urinary bladder; they applied the conservative method, including measures directed at the increase of general resistance of the organism and local action on the repair regeneration with pharmacological stimuli. The therapeutic mixture consisting of a 0.9% metacyl solution, novocain, hydrocortisone, vitamin B12 and antibiotics was administered intravesically, transvaginally and prevesically. The use of this method permitted recovery in 85% of the patients in the course of 1 to 3 months. The same principles were applied in surgical treatment, particularly in the patients with ulcers with protracted healing.
