N2  - The fever induced by E. coli pyrogen (LPS) is accompanied by a rise of FFA and glycerol level. All tested antipyretics inhibited both thermogenesis and lipolysis produced by LPS. These results suggest that the antipyretic effect of antipyretic drugs is not confined to their action on heat dissipating mechanisms, but may also be exerted by a depression of lipid metabolism.
